Description: pvr: cache render states for dynamic rendering
 With dynamic rendering every vkCmdBeginRendering gets a new render state:
 pvr_arch_render_state_setup() allocates the PPP state, compiles and uploads
 the SPM end-of-tile program and allocates the SPM background object state,
 and the first job of the render creates a render target dataset (HWRT
 dataset, local free list and their buffers). All of it is destroyed when the
 command buffer is reset or freed. Under zink, which only uses dynamic
 rendering, this happens for every render pass: each one creates a new HWRT
 dataset and free list, and several buffer objects are created, mapped and
 unmapped per submit.
 .
 Keep the render states of dynamic rendering that have no references on a
 per-device list in order of use, each with a key of everything
 pvr_arch_render_state_setup() and the dataset creation read: width, height,
 layers, sample count, output register count, tile buffer count and SPM
 scratch buffer size. The list can hold several entries with the same key.
 vkCmdBeginRendering first looks for a render state with the same key in the
 graphics sub commands of its own command buffer and takes another reference
 on it. Passes of one command buffer run in order, so a command buffer with
 several passes of the same size shares one render state and dataset.
 Otherwise it takes the most recently used idle render state with that key
 off the list, or sets up a new one. Secondary command buffers that continue
 a render pass only take idle render states.
 .
 A render state is never handed to a second command buffer while it is in
 use: the dataset slot and the pending fragment job of its datasets are
 updated without a lock and are meant for one user at a time. Freeing the sub
 command drops the reference. When the last reference is dropped, the render
 state goes back to the list, which keeps 16 entries and destroys the least
 recently used one beyond that, or it is destroyed right away if a dataset
 still waits for its fragment job (need_frag). The list is emptied at device
 destruction. A command buffer that is submitted again while its previous
 submission still executes keeps using the render states it holds. Render
 passes with framebuffers are unchanged.
 .
 Error paths in vkCmdBeginRendering free the unused render state, and a
 failure in pvr_arch_mrt_load_ops_setup() leaves render state and render info
 to the sub command that already owns them.
 .
 Only for this downstream stack; not intended for upstream submission.
